-- title:
--   Lower bound for dim H¹ by invariants and Frobenius kernel
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and $G$ a finite group, $A$ a representation of $G$ over $k$ that is finite-dimensional as a $k$-module, and $S$ a normal subgroup of $G$ with finite quotient $G/S$. Assume given $t \in S$ with $S \le \langle t\rangle$ (the subgroup of integer powers of $t$), and $\varphi \in G$ whose class in $G/S$ is such that every element of $G/S$ is an integer power of it; let $f = \operatorname{ord}(\varphi S)$. Assume further natural numbers $m$ and $j$ with $\varphi^{-1} t \varphi = t^{m}$, with $\varphi t \varphi^{-1} \in \langle t\rangle$, and with $\varphi^{f} = t^{j}$. Finally impose four vanishing conditions: the endomorphisms $\sum_{i<\operatorname{ord}(t)} \rho(t^{i})$, $\sum_{i<j} \rho(t^{i})$ and $\sum_{i<f} \rho(\varphi^{i})$ of $A$ all vanish, and the norm endomorphism of the $G/S$-representation on $A^{S}$ (given by `Rep.quotientToInvariants`) vanishes. Write $F$ for the endomorphism of $A/\operatorname{im}(\rho(t)-1)$ induced by $\rho(\varphi)$, which is well defined by the hypothesis $\varphi t \varphi^{-1} \in \langle t\rangle$ (`frobeniusOnCoinvariants`). Then $$\dim_k A^{G} + \dim_k \ker(m\,F - 1) \le \dim_k H^{1}(G,A).$$
--
--   This is a lower bound for $\dim H^1$ of the shape complementary to the local Euler-characteristic upper bound, in the finite-group model of a tamely ramified local Galois group: $S$ plays the role of the inertia subgroup generated by $t$ and $\varphi$ that of a Frobenius lift, the four vanishing hypotheses expressing that the representation is of sufficient depth. It is used in the companion bound [`groupCohomology.finrank_invariants_add_finrank_invariants_dualTwist_le_finrank_inflationImage`](thm.html#groupCohomology.finrank_invariants_add_finrank_invariants_dualTwist_le_finrank_inflationImage).
